        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-13T05:20:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jooyung, do you think checking it on apex.native_shared_libs should be _instead_ of or in _addition_ to this check?\n\nIf it is the former, then I think it will be difficult to implement in Bazel. We effectively have to scan the entire tree for apex targets, look at its native_shared_libs for stub libraries, and verify that there are no duplicates for stub libraries (The test apex question still remains though).\n\nI think another advantage of implementing this as a local check is that makes the stub/impl selection logic more precise in bp2build. In Soong we dedupe apex variants, but in Bazel we can build variants for each apex_available without incurring significant performance loss. If there is a guarantee that each stub library has a single apex available, we can make the bp2build stub selection logic like such for a _specific_ apex variant of an rdep\n- if apex is in the stub library\u0027s apex_available, use impl\n- otherwise stubs",
